# No em dashes

This is an example of a house-style rule: a small, concrete, checkable preference that the agent applies everywhere. Swap it for your own (for example "no exclamation marks", "sentence case headings", "no emoji").

Never use Unicode U+2014. Do not type it, paste it, or substitute "fancy" punctuation. This applies to chat, markdown, code comments, shipped copy, commits and rules.

Use commas, brackets, a full stop or a colon. A hyphen `-` is fine as a simple separator. Use an en dash only for a true numeric range.

When editing a line that already has an em dash, rewrite that line to remove it.
